PRODUCT DESCRIPTION
Issue: 20/05/2026, Rev. 6
Material no.: LA01

Lactic Acid – E 270

Description:
Lactic acid from natural fermentation of natural carbohydrates. Yields the L(+) form preferred for its better metabolization. Lactic acid is an organic acid occurring naturally in the human body and in fermented foods. It is typically used in a wide range of food and beverages as a mild acidity regulator, flavor enhancer, or in brine to prepare meat and fish. This product is commercially available in aqueous solutions in a concentration range from 1-2% (and up to 2-5% upon request). Does not require pre-dilution before use and is not hazardous or corrosive in these concentrations. Final concentration is available on the batch release report (as CoA). The product is stable in normal storage conditions.

Ingredients:
Water, Lactic Acid (E 270)

Production:
- Natural fermentation from non-GMO, QPS listed lactic acid food cultures (non-synthetical).
- Product ready to use out of bag/container.
- Packed as a liquid in food-grade bags.
- All packaging materials are food grade and assembled in aseptic environments (ISO8 facilities).
- Product is produced under (EC) 178/2002, (EC) 852/2004 in BioCulture Nordic’s good manufacturing practice and HACCP-protocols.

Direction for use:
- To be applied to food. Typically used as mild acidity regulator.
- Application in animal-derived foods (like fish/meat) is typically added directly to suspensions like brine and applied through injection (stitch pump), soaking, or surface glazing.
- Refer to the Food and Feed Portal (FIP-portal) for the specific food categories where Lactic Acid may be applied.
- Product does not require pre-dilution by user.
- Authorized Lactic Acid E 270 usage for surface treatment and organic regulation in European animal foods. Please refer to (EC) 101/2013.

GMO & Regulations:
- Regulation (EC) No. 1829/2003 and Regulation (EC) 1830/2003 of the European Parliament and the Council of 22 September 2003. The lactic acid strain is from a natural source and has Qualified Presumed Safety status (QPS listed).
- GMO-free, vegan-suitable, and free from synthetic preservatives.

Certificates:
- Kosher and Halal certificates are available upon request.

Liability:
All technical advice is provided to the best of our knowledge. However, we do not accept any liability for improper application.
Lactic acid and the fermentation from lactic acid bacteria have a long history of safe use in food. Labeling and use may vary from country to country.

Service:
Please contact BioCulture Nordic for further guidance and instructions at contact@bioculturenordic.com.
